META VIOLATION — the artifact inverts the contract it claims to express, and its authoring
furniture is present but hollow.

SUBSTANCE. session-notes-continuity.md MUST-1 requires the FIRST continuity artifact read to be
a ROOT one and states that mtime ordering is exactly the trap (a freshly-touched narrative
outranks a stale-but-authoritative aggregate). This artifact writes recency in as the intake
ORDER ("begin with whichever continuity artifact was written most recently", "the more recent
of the two should ordinarily be preferred"), which is that trap stated as the remedy. It then
inverts MUST-2: a windowed read is licensed outright ("a quick orienting read of the opening
section is usually sufficient", "the agent may reasonably window the read"), where the parent
carries a structural `block` on exactly that parameter.

AUTHORING DEFECTS, all of the CONTENT of the furniture, never its absence. The section is
headed "MUST Rules" while the modal throughout is should / generally / normally / usually /
may — no MUST, no MUST NOT, no BLOCKED token. The DO/DO-NOT block restates its own headings in
prose instead of showing two calls whose outcomes differ; nothing in it is matchable. The
BLOCKED list is abstract paraphrase of a disposition ("Reading continuity material
excessively") rather than agent speech a session could be caught saying. The `**Why:**` names a
budget cost and then closes on "the freshest artifact is usually the one that describes the
current state of things anyway" — the belief under test restated as its own justification.

NOT THE DEFECT. Frontmatter, `## Origin`, the Wiring block and its field set are all present
and well-formed, and both poles carry them; the `advisory` severity follows from the inverted
premise and is not a separate finding. The two poles share a heading skeleton, one numbered
clause each, and sit at a 1.07x size ratio, so nothing about FORM separates them.
